      "body": "## Purpose\n\nWarns Apple Silicon (vLLM-Metal) users that some models cannot be loaded:\n\n1. vLLM-Metal loads weights through MLX, which requires `.safetensors` checkpoints.\n2. Some models, such as `facebook/opt-125m`, only ship legacy `.bin` weights and\n   fail with `FileNotFoundError: No safetensors found in ...`.\n3. Use a model that ships safetensors instead, for example `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B` (the\n   default model for `vllm serve`) or an MLX-optimized model from\n   [mlx-community](https://huggingface.co/mlx-community) such as\n   `mlx-community/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct-4bit`.\n\nDocumentation-only change; no code is touched.\n\n## Why the note moved\n\nThis PR was previously open as #57739 and put the note in the general quickstart\nguide. @mgoin closed it with \"This detail doesn't belong in the general docs\",\nwhich is right: the note only applies to Apple Silicon users running vLLM-Metal,\nand it made the quickstart example conditional on the reader's platform.\n\nThis revision moves the note into the Apple Silicon tab of the CPU installation\npage (`docs/getting_started/installation/cpu.apple.inc.md`), directly after the\nvLLM-Metal tip, and drops the quickstart change entirely.\n\n## Relationship to #62747\n\n#50165 was closed as not planned in favour of #62747, which replaces\n`facebook/opt-125m` with `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B` across the doc examples. That\naddresses the same underlying problem for the general examples.\n\nThis PR does not touch any of the pages #62747 changes, so the two do not\noverlap. What is left over is the Apple Silicon installation page, which still\ndoes not mention that the model needs to ship safetensors for MLX to load it.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `markdownlint-cli2 --config tools/pre_commit/.markdownlint.yaml` on the\n  changed file: 0 issues.\n- Checked that the note renders inside the `installation` snippet block, which\n  `docs/getting_started/installation/cpu.md` includes under the \"Apple silicon\"\n  tab.\n\n## Test Result\n\n- 1 file changed, 3 lines added.\n",
